From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kangaroo maintainers
Date: 2026-10-16
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: g-ir-scanner cache disable + dump-program link/run hardening

The first 0016-enabled CI run pushed all three MINGW environments past
the pkg-config path crash and the GNU-ld dump-link stall, and exposed
the next toolchain-specific failure layer of the introspection tail
(edges ~8570/8577, the last steps of the whole build):

CLANG64 - the WebKit-6.0.gir scan aborted at scanner startup:

  File ".../giscanner/transformer.py", line 140, in register_include
  ... transformer.py:232 x4 (recursive include resolution)
  File ".../giscanner/cachestore.py", line 166, in load
    fd = open(store_filename, 'rb')
  PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied:
  'C:/Users/runneradmin/.cache/g-ir-scanner/7536ef06...'

gobject-introspection 1.86.0 (as shipped by MSYS2 - the traceback line
numbers match the upstream sources byte for byte) has NO cross-process
locking in its parse cache: CacheStore writes entries with tempfile +
shutil.move (non-atomic on Windows) and load() only tolerates ENOENT;
every other OSError aborts the whole scan. Ninja runs the
JavaScriptCore / WebKit / WebProcessExtension scanner edges in
parallel, all sharing the one %USERPROFILE%\.cache\g-ir-scanner
directory, and the freshly-written multi-MB .gir parse pickles are
held open by the CI machines' real-time antivirus just long enough for
the concurrent WebKit scan to hit a sharing violation. g-i's own
utils.rmtree() docstring documents the very same virus-scanner
interference. Setting GI_SCANNER_DISABLE_CACHE (any value; the code is
a presence check in CacheStore._get_cachedir) makes _directory None,
turning load()/store() into no-ops: no shared files, no lock windows,
no stale entries carried across CI runs. The cost is re-parsing the
include .gir XML per scan - seconds against a multi-hour build.

CLANGARM64 - the WebKit-6.0 introspection dump program exited with
status 3221226505 (0xC0000409, fail-fast: clang lowers
__stack_chk_fail to int 0x29 on Windows, and the UCRT
_invalid_parameter handler fail-fasts the same way). Two mechanisms
are already ruled out by the same CI log: the WebProcessExtension
dump, which loads the very same libwebkitgtk-6.0 DLL, succeeded (its
vapigen edge started right after), so DLL loading and static
initialization are healthy; and glib's gmodule resolves the get_type
functions through find_in_any_module() (a Toolhelp snapshot walk over
all loaded modules' export tables), so exe-level export configuration
is irrelevant. What remains is the dump run itself: ~200 UI-process
get_type functions, their complete class_init chains and the property
default-value evaluation, driven on a main thread whose PE default
stack reservation is 2 MiB - a quarter of the 8 MiB Linux default
WebKit code is tuned against. Reserve a 16 MiB stack for the dump
program (purely virtual, committed on demand, dump program only).

UCRT64 - the build stalled again after the 0016 linker switch (no log
tail provided; the Round-42 watchdog will name the live command line
next time). With the dump link now on lld, the first untested step on
UCRT64 is the same dump-program run, so the same hardening applies.

Additionally set GI_SCANNER_DEBUG=save-temps for the scanner runs: on
any scan failure g-ir-scanner then keeps its tmp-introspect*/
directory - the dump program, functions.txt and the partial dump.xml,
whose last <class>/<interface> element names the type being processed
when the dump program died. That is the single most valuable artifact
for debugging dump-program crashes on CI machines, at the cost of a
few hundred KB per scan.

All changes are WIN32-only (inside the gi_scanner_env block of the
GI_INTROSPECT macro); Linux builds are untouched.
---
--- a/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake
@@ -528,7 +528,39 @@
         # while lld (installed alongside llvm-ar/llvm-ranlib) links it
         # instantly and is the linker the CLANG environments use for
         # every other target anyway.
-        list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "LDFLAGS=-fuse-ld=lld")
+        # The dump program also loads the multi-hundred-MB libwebkitgtk
+        # DLL and drives the complete GType registration of the scanned
+        # API (hundreds of class_init chains plus property default value
+        # evaluation) on its main thread. The PE default stack
+        # reservation is 2 MiB, a quarter of the 8 MiB Linux default
+        # WebKit code is tuned against; reserve 16 MiB instead (a purely
+        # virtual reservation, committed on demand, and only the dump
+        # program is affected).
+        list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "LDFLAGS=-fuse-ld=lld -Wl,--stack,0x1000000")
+        # g-ir-scanner's cross-process parse cache (giscanner/cachestore.py)
+        # has no locking at all in gobject-introspection 1.86.0: entries
+        # are written via tempfile + shutil.move (non-atomic on Windows)
+        # and load() only tolerates ENOENT. Ninja runs the JavaScriptCore
+        # / WebKit / WebProcessExtension scans in parallel over the one
+        # shared %USERPROFILE%\.cache\g-ir-scanner directory, and the CI
+        # machines' real-time antivirus holds freshly-written multi-MB
+        # pickles open long enough for a concurrent reader to hit a
+        # sharing violation (PermissionError [Errno 13], observed
+        # aborting the WebKit-6.0 scan at startup on CLANG64). Disabling
+        # the cache costs a re-parse of the include .gir files per scan
+        # (seconds) and removes the entire failure class: no shared
+        # files, no lock windows, no stale entries carried across CI
+        # runs.
+        list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "GI_SCANNER_DISABLE_CACHE=1")
+        # Keep the tmp-introspect*/ directory (dump program,
+        # functions.txt, partial dump.xml) when a scan fails:
+        # GI_SCANNER_DEBUG=save-temps makes g-ir-scanner skip its
+        # post-run cleanup, preserving the crash scene - the last
+        # <class>/<interface> element of a partial dump.xml names the
+        # type being processed when the dump program died, the single
+        # most valuable artifact for debugging dump-program crashes on
+        # CI machines. Costs a few hundred KB per scan.
+        list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "GI_SCANNER_DEBUG=save-temps")
     endif ()
     add_custom_command(
         OUTPUT "${gir_path}"
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kangaroo maintainers
Date: 2026-10-16
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: skip the heavy WebKit2/JSC/Skia initialization inside the gir dump program (WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE)

The 0017-enabled CI run pushed CLANG64 past the scanner cache crash,
unmasking the same dump-program failure CLANGARM64 had shown the round
before: the WebKit-6.0 introspection dump program exited 3221226505
(0xC0000409 fail-fast). The 16 MiB stack reserve from 0017 did not
cure it, and the WebProcessExtension dump (which links the very same
libwebkitgtk DLL and runs the same gdump.c runtime) succeeded on both
machines at the same edge - isolating the failure to something the
WebKit-6.0 dump does and the WEPE dump does not.

That difference is in the class_init chains: gdump.c's dump_type does
g_type_class_ref(type) for every scanned type, running each class_init
body. A source audit of the whole public API surface (UIProcess/API
glib + gtk) finds exactly one family of non-GLib code executed there:
seven class_init bodies (WebKitNetworkSession, WebKitInputMethodContext,
WebKitWebContext, WebKitSettings, WebKitUserContentFilterStore,
WebKitUserContentManager, WebKitWebsiteDataManager) call
WebKit::webkitInitialize() first, which runs the full
InitializeWebKit2() (JSC::initialize, WTF main-thread setup, WebCore
atom strings, populateJITOperations) plus SkGraphics::Init() inside
the bare C-linked dump process. On Linux this incidental execution is
survivable and therefore invisible; on this port it is the crash
frontier. Nothing in a .gir depends on that initialization.

Fix (both changes, Windows-scoped):
  1. WebKitInitialize.cpp: under OS(WINDOWS), webkitInitialize() returns
     early when WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE is set; applications (and every
     Linux build) keep the upstream behavior byte-for-byte.
  2. FindGI.cmake: the scanner environment exports
     WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE=1; the dump program inherits it through
     g-ir-scanner's subprocess (no env= override there), so every dump
     run (JSC / WebKit / WebProcessExtension) skips the heavy init.

The gir content is unaffected: the dump still class-refs every type,
collects the full hierarchy, properties (specs and default values) and
signals; only the heavyweight process-global initialization is skipped.

Verification in this round: pure-replay of the consolidated 5-patch
series on a fresh tarball reproduces the 18-step tree byte-exactly
(diff -r empty); sentinels added to PKGBUILD prepare() for both hunks
(bidirectional: consolidated-tree passes, 0017-era tree triggers).

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitInitialize.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitInitialize.cpp
index bdd42db..f0bd7ed 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitInitialize.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitInitialize.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include "WebKit2Initialize.h"
 #include <JavaScriptCore/RemoteInspector.h>
 #include <JavaScriptCore/RemoteInspectorServer.h>
+#include <glib.h>
 #include <limits>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <skia/core/SkGraphics.h>
@@ -107,6 +108,26 @@ void webkitInitialize()
     std::call_once(onceFlag, [] {
 #if USE(SYSPROF_CAPTURE)
         SysprofAnnotator::createIfNeeded("WebKit (UI)"_s);
+#endif
+#if OS(WINDOWS)
+        // MinGW port: g-ir-scanner's dump program class-refs the public API
+        // types inside a bare C-linked process to collect the GType table,
+        // property specs and signal list for the .gir. Seven public class_init
+        // bodies (NetworkSession, InputMethodContext, WebContext, Settings,
+        // UserContentFilterStore, UserContentManager, WebsiteDataManager) call
+        // webkitInitialize() first, so on Linux the dump incidentally runs the
+        // full WebKit2/JSC/Skia initialization from there and survives. On
+        // Windows the same heavyweight initialization is not needed for the
+        // dump (nothing in a .gir depends on it) and is the dump-program crash
+        // frontier on this port (0xC0000409 fail-fast, CLANG64 and
+        // CLANGARM64, at the exact edge where the WebProcessExtension dump -
+        // whose class_inits never call webkitInitialize() - succeeds).
+        // FindGI.cmake exports WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE=1 for the scanner runs;
+        // the dump program inherits it and skips the heavy initialization
+        // here. Real applications on Windows (and every build on Linux)
+        // keep the upstream behavior unchanged.
+        if (g_getenv("WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE"))
+            return;
 #endif
         InitializeWebKit2();
 
diff --git a/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake b/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake
index 358e436..3271c5b 100644
--- a/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/FindGI.cmake
@@ -561,6 +561,22 @@ function(GI_INTROSPECT namespace nsversion header)
         # most valuable artifact for debugging dump-program crashes on
         # CI machines. Costs a few hundred KB per scan.
         list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "GI_SCANNER_DEBUG=save-temps")
+        # Round 44: the dump program class-refs every public API type
+        # (gdump.c: dump_type -> g_type_class_ref) to collect the GType
+        # table, property specs and signal list. Seven public class_init
+        # bodies call WebKit::webkitInitialize() first, so the dump run
+        # would execute the full WebKit2/JSC/Skia initialization inside
+        # the bare C-linked dump process. On Linux this incidental
+        # execution survives; on Windows it is the dump-program crash
+        # frontier (0xC0000409 fail-fast, CLANG64 and CLANGARM64, while
+        # the WebProcessExtension dump - whose class_inits never call
+        # webkitInitialize() - succeeds on the same machines). Nothing
+        # in a .gir depends on that initialization, so export
+        # WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE=1 for the scanner environment: the dump
+        # program inherits it and WebKitInitialize.cpp (OS(WINDOWS)
+        # guarded) skips the heavy initialization there. Real Windows
+        # applications are unaffected.
+        list(APPEND gi_scanner_env "WEBKIT_GIR_DUMP_MODE=1")
     endif ()
     add_custom_command(
         OUTPUT "${gir_path}"
